Issues
Integrating the Memory, Stack, and Queue components required coordination because all three components use the shared data-memory space.
Changes to CPU and UI components had to be coordinated between team members to avoid conflicts during integration.
Stack and Queue operations require careful management of their allocated RAM regions to prevent data overlap.
Additional validation was required to ensure that queue pointer updates and circular wrap-around behaved correctly.
  
Concerns
Future additions to the simulator will increase the amount of shared CPU, memory, and UI code that needs to be maintained.
The fixed-size queue limits the number of elements that can be stored at one time.
Increasing the instruction set may require additional changes to opcode decoding, execution logic, testing, and UI representation.
As more simulator components are integrated, maintaining clear separation between modules will become increasingly important.

